Title: TSM Enchanting crafting window stays empty, Craft button crashes on enchants
Why: TSM maps each enchant to a retail scroll item the Forever client lacks, so the recipe scan retried forever. Unknown scroll items are now ignored so enchants scan as plain spells. Enchants then have no result item, so they are not in the craft DB; the Craft button no longer asserts on that.

=== FILE TradeSkillMaster\LibTSMService\Source\Profession\Internal\Data.lua
--- OLD
	return EnchantData.Recipes[spellId] or SalvageData.MassMill[spellId] or EnchantData.QualityRecipes[spellId] or nil
--- NEW
	local result = EnchantData.Recipes[spellId] or SalvageData.MassMill[spellId] or EnchantData.QualityRecipes[spellId] or nil
	-- LOCAL FIX: enchant scroll items don't exist in the Forever client, which makes the profession scan retry forever
	if LibTSMService.IsForever() and type(result) == "string" and not C_Item.GetItemInfoInstant(tonumber(strmatch(result, "^i:(%d+)"))) then
		return nil
	end
	return result
=== END

=== FILE TradeSkillMaster\LibTSMService\Source\Crafting\Internal\Craft.lua
=== INLINE
--- OLD
local craftItemString = CraftInfoDB.GetItemString(craftString) --[[@as string?]]
--- NEW
local craftItemString = CraftInfoDB.HasCraftString(craftString) and CraftInfoDB.GetItemString(craftString) or nil --[[@as string?]] -- LOCAL FIX: enchants (no result item) aren't in the craft DB on Forever
=== END
